SRC/eff_gshell -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  selectfile.c, 2026-09-26.  select_file() and new_dir() read one key with  read() and never looked at what read() returned.  At the end of the  input the key was left as it was -- the letter after the last one  listed -- so the menu took it as a wrong letter, beeped and redrew  itself, for ever: `editor /dd/SYS < /nil' drew its menu 4,234 times  in 20 seconds before it was stopped.  Now the end of  the input leaves the menu as `!' does, and new_dir() gives up rather  than use a key it never read.  Two lines.  Only CMDS/editor was rebuilt from it (recipe `editor', -qm).  gshell,  assembler and compiler share selectfile.c and would take the same fix  when rebuilt.  The original is selectfile.c.ori; the .r files beside  it are the archive's own and were not touched.